module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.CechPullbackDerived
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.PushforwardCommutesCompletionKoszulTower
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.InternalHom.DerivedPushforwardOfInternalHom
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# `Rf_*(K^∧) = (Rf_*K)^∧` for an arbitrary object, from the Čech formula

[Stacks, Tag 0A0G] asserts that `Rf_*` commutes with derived completion,
`Rf_*(K^∧) = (Rf_*K)^∧`, for an **arbitrary** `K ∈ D(𝒪')`, and [Stacks, Tag 0A0I] writes that
identity down as Equation 52.7.0.1. This file proves it for an arbitrary `K`, at a pair of
sheaves of ideals generated by finitely many global sections with `g_i = f^♯(t_i)` — the regime
the source's own proof reduces to — as an **explicit isomorphism**, built from three
identifications and nothing else:

1. derived completion along `ℐ' = (g_1, …, g_r)` **is** `R𝓗om_{𝒪'}(Č(g), -)`, the Čech
   completion of [Stacks, Tag 099B]: `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.reflectorIsoCompletionFunctor`;
2. `Lf^*Č(𝒪, t) ≅ Č(𝒪', g)`:
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedPullbackExtendedAlternatingCechIso`;
3. the adjoint formula `Rf_* R𝓗om_{𝒪'}(Lf^*A, M) ≅ R𝓗om_𝒪(A, Rf_*M)`, for arbitrary `A` and
   `M`: `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPushforward.derivedPushforwardSheafHomObjIso`;

followed by (1) again on the target site, at `Rf_*K`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedPushforwardCechCompletionIso`:
  `Rf_* R𝓗om_{𝒪'}(Č(g), K) ≅ R𝓗om_𝒪(Č(t), Rf_*K)`, the display read at the Čech completions.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedPushforwardDerivedCompletionGeneratedIdealSheafIso`:
  **`Rf_*(K^∧) ≅ (Rf_*K)^∧`** for an arbitrary `K`, at the two generated ideal sheaves.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedPushforward_obj_of_isZero`: `Rf_*` carries a zero
  object to a zero object, from the adjunction alone.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedCompletion_derivedPushforward_of_isZero`:
  **`Rf_*` carries a completion-acyclic object to a completion-acyclic object** — if `K^∧ = 0`
  then `(Rf_*K)^∧ = 0`.

## Implementation notes

*The relation between the two ideal sheaves.* What the proof uses is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.PushGlobalSectionsCompatible f t g`, that `g_i` is `f^♯(t_i)` on
sections over every object of the target site — the source's own relation between the two
generating families, "Then `ℐ'` is generated by `g_i = f^♯(f_i)`". The weaker
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.PushforwardIdealCompatible` between the generated ideal sheaves is
not enough and is not assumed: the pulled-back Čech complex needs the generators to correspond.

*Comparison with the derived-limit form.*
`RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedPushforward_derivedCompletion_generatedIdealSheaf`
of `PushforwardCommutesCompletionHomTower.lean` proves the same conclusion at the same
generality by presenting both completions as derived limits of Koszul Hom towers. Uniqueness of
derived limits is non-canonical, so that gives only `Nonempty (Rf_*(K^∧) ≅ (Rf_*K)^∧)`, and it
assumes countable coproducts
`Limits.HasCoproduct ((koszulPowerSystem · ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q).obj)` of `D(𝒪)` on either site.
Here each of the three identifications above is a named isomorphism, so their composite is a
`def`, and no coproduct in a derived category is needed: the only colimit used is the sequential
colimit of Koszul *complexes* which the Čech complex already is, inside `CechPullback.lean`.

*Objects, not the canonical map.* The conclusion is the display as the source writes it,
`Rf_*(K^∧) = (Rf_*K)^∧`. Identifying the isomorphism with
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison` additionally needs the
adjoint formula to be compatible with the map a complex over `𝒪` induces on derived internal
Hom, which is the right-unitor coherence of [Stacks, Tag 07A4] in the derived category. The two
completion maps are compatible with (1) on either site
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionUnit_comp_reflectorToCompletionFunctor`), so that
coherence is the only step between this isomorphism and the canonical comparison map.

*The completion-acyclic form.* An isomorphism of two objects does not descend along a covering
family, but vanishing does (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isZero_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory`), so
the completion-acyclic form is the half of the display that a local-to-global argument on the
target site can use. The local-to-global statement for a sheaf of ideals of finite type,
`RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_inverseImageIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType`
of `PushforwardCommutesCompletionLocalToGlobal.lean`, instead descends the invertibility of the
**canonical comparison map**, which is local by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory`, through the restriction coherence
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_localized`; it uses
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal_inverseImageIdealSheaf` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf_generatedIdealSheaf` to identify
`ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` on the slice over `f.u V` with the ideal generated by the pushed generators
of `ℐ|_V`.

The derived direct image of a morphism of ringed sites carries no `Additive` instance in this
library, so `CategoryTheory.Functor.map_isZero` is unavailable; the adjunction `Lf^* ⊣ Rf_*`
gives the vanishing of `Rf_*` on zero objects directly.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0I)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedPullbackPushforwardAdjunction

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] hasFiniteBiproducts_sheafOfModules
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat
attribute [local instance] isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf
attribute [local instance] hasLeftDerivedFunctor_pullbackOnHomotopy

section ZeroObject

variable {X Y : RingedSite.{u, u, u}}
  [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [Y.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  (f : RingedSite.Hom X Y)

/-- **The derived direct image of a zero object is zero.** `Rf_*` is a right adjoint, so a map
into `Rf_*A` is a map into `A` after transposition, and there is only one of those when `A` is
zero; so the identity of `Rf_*A` is zero.

This is the step that additivity of `Rf_*` would otherwise supply:
`CategoryTheory.Functor.map_isZero` needs `PreservesZeroMorphisms`, and the derived direct image
of a morphism of ringed *sites* carries no such instance in this library. The adjunction
`Lf^* ⊣ Rf_*` of [Stacks, Tag 07A6] gives the conclusion with no additivity at all. -/
theorem isZero_derivedPushforward_obj_of_isZero
    {A : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))}
    (hA : IsZero A) :
    IsZero ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj A) := by
  rw [IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero]
  exact ((derivedPullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv
    ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj A) A).symm.injective
      (hA.eq_of_tgt _ _)

end ZeroObject

section Cech

variable {X Y : RingedSite.{u, u, u}}
  [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u} X.O).Additive]
  [∀ A, ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u} X.O).obj A).Additive]
  [∀ (K₁ K₂ : HomologicalComplex
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} X.O))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)),
    HomologicalComplex.HasMapBifunctor K₁ K₂ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.O)
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)]
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}]
  [HasSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [Y.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u} Y.O).Additive]
  [∀ A, ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u} Y.O).obj A).Additive]
  [∀ (K₁ K₂ : HomologicalComplex
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} Y.O))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)),
    HomologicalComplex.HasMapBifunctor K₁ K₂ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor Y.O)
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)]
  [HasWeakSheafify Y.J CommRingCat.{u}]
  (f : RingedSite.Hom X Y) {r : ℕ}
  (t : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (Y.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
  (g : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
  (hg : PushGlobalSectionsCompatible f t g)

include hg in
/-- **`Rf_* R𝓗om_{𝒪'}(Č(g), K) ≅ R𝓗om_𝒪(Č(t), Rf_*K)`** for an arbitrary `K ∈ D(𝒪')`: the
display of [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] read at the Čech completions of [Stacks, Tag 099B].

The first factor rewrites the source's Čech complex as the derived inverse image of the target's,
by `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedPullbackExtendedAlternatingCechIso`; the second is the
adjoint formula `Rf_* R𝓗om_{𝒪'}(Lf^*A, M) ≅ R𝓗om_𝒪(A, Rf_*M)`, which holds for arbitrary `A`
and `M`. -/
def derivedPushforwardCechCompletionIso
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    (derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj ((completionFunctor X g).obj K) ≅
      (completionFunctor Y t).obj ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj K) :=
  (derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).mapIso
      (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).mapIso
        (derivedPullbackExtendedAlternatingCechIso f t g hg).op).app K) ≪≫
    Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPushforward.derivedPushforwardSheafHomObjIso
      f.toRingedToposSiteHom f.isMorphismOfSites
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (extendedAlternatingCech Y t)) K

include hg in
/-- **[Stacks, Tags 0A0G and 0A0I] for an arbitrary object, at two sheaves of ideals generated by
finitely many global sections.** Let `f : (Sh(𝒟), 𝒪') ⟶ (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪)` be a morphism of ringed
sites, let `t_1, …, t_r` be global sections of `𝒪` generating `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪`, let `g_i = f^♯(t_i)`
generate `ℐ' ⊂ 𝒪'`, and let `K ∈ D(𝒪')` be **arbitrary**. Then

`Rf_*(K^∧) ≅ (Rf_*K)^∧`:

`Rf_*` commutes with derived completion. Both derived completion functors are the reflector of
[Stacks, Tag 099F], produced from the generators by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`, so no part
of that tag is an input.

The reflector at a globally generated ideal sheaf **is** the Čech completion
`R𝓗om(Č(-), -)` of [Stacks, Tag 099B]
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.reflectorIsoCompletionFunctor`), the source's Čech complex is the
derived inverse image of the target's, and the adjoint formula moves `Rf_*` across the internal
Hom. No countable coproduct in a derived category is assumed, and the isomorphism is produced
rather than shown to exist; see the module documentation for the comparison with the
derived-limit form. -/
@[stacks 0A0G "`Rf_*` commutes with derived completion, `Rf_*(K^∧) = (Rf_*K)^∧`, for an \
**arbitrary** object `K` of `D(𝒪')`, at `ℐ = (t_1, …, t_r) ⊂ 𝒪` and \
`ℐ' = (f^♯t_1, …, f^♯t_r) ⊂ 𝒪'` generated by finitely many global sections of the two structure \
sheaves — the regime the source's own proof reduces to, and the regime in which \
[Stacks, Tag 099F] is available here, so that both derived completion functors are built from \
those generators and no part of that tag is an input. The display is produced as an explicit \
isomorphism from three identifications: derived completion along a globally generated ideal \
sheaf is the Čech completion of [Stacks, Tag 099B]; `Lf^*Č(𝒪, t) ≅ Č(𝒪', g)`; and the adjoint \
formula `Rf_* R𝓗om_{𝒪'}(Lf^*A, M) ≅ R𝓗om_𝒪(A, Rf_*M)` at arbitrary `A` and `M`. Restrictions \
on the data only: the object is arbitrary, and no countable coproduct in a derived category is \
assumed"]
def derivedPushforwardDerivedCompletionGeneratedIdealSheafIso
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    (derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj
        ((derivedCompletion X (generatedIdealSheaf g)).obj K) ≅
      (derivedCompletion Y (generatedIdealSheaf t)).obj
        ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj K) :=
  (derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).mapIso
      (reflectorIsoCompletionFunctor X g K) ≪≫
    derivedPushforwardCechCompletionIso f t g hg K ≪≫
    (reflectorIsoCompletionFunctor Y t
      ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj K)).symm

include hg in
/-- **`Rf_*` carries a completion-acyclic object to a completion-acyclic object.** If `K^∧ = 0`
then `(Rf_*K)^∧ = 0`, at two sheaves of ideals generated by finitely many global sections with
`g_i = f^♯(t_i)`.

This is the form in which the display enters a local-to-global argument on the target site:
vanishing in `D(𝒪)` is a local condition
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isZero_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory`), while an isomorphism of two
objects is not. -/
theorem isZero_derivedCompletion_derivedPushforward_of_isZero
    {K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))}
    (hK : IsZero ((derivedCompletion X (generatedIdealSheaf g)).obj K)) :
    IsZero ((derivedCompletion Y (generatedIdealSheaf t)).obj
      ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj K)) :=
  (isZero_derivedPushforward_obj_of_isZero f hK).of_iso
    (derivedPushforwardDerivedCompletionGeneratedIdealSheafIso f t g hg K).symm

end Cech

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
